<doc id="146002" url="https://jv.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=146002" title="Karen Brodkin">
Karen Brodkin

Karen Helen Brodkin ya iku ahli &lt;a href="antropologi"&gt;antropologi&lt;/a&gt; wanita saka &lt;a href="New%20York"&gt;New York&lt;/a&gt; City, &lt;a href="Am%C3%A9rikah%20Sar%C3%A9kat"&gt;Amérikah Sarékat&lt;/a&gt;, kalairan taun 1941. Karen Brodkin kuliah sarjana (BA) ing &lt;a href="Brandei%20University"&gt;Brandei University&lt;/a&gt; taun 1963. Sabanjuré pasca sarjana (MA) ing &lt;a href="Harvard%20University"&gt;Harvard University&lt;/a&gt; taun 1964 lan doktor ing &lt;a href="University%20of%20Michigan"&gt;University of Michigan&lt;/a&gt; taun 1971. Karen naté nglakoni panlitian lapangan antropologis ing Carolina lor (1980an) lan &lt;a href="Los%20Angeles"&gt;Los Angeles&lt;/a&gt; (1990). Dhéwéké wis nulis karya-karya antropologis kaya déné ‘Engels revisited: women, the organization of production, and private property’ ing jurnal Women, Culture, and Society, Sisters and Wives: The Past and Future of Sexual Equality (1979), Caring by the Hour (1988), lan How Jews Became White Folks and What That Says about Race in America (1998). Karen kawentar amarga fokus panlitiané ing bab antropologi fèminis, khususé jénder, krabatan, ètnologis lan téori fèminis, rasialisasi, lan budaya kapitalis kontemporér ing Amérika Lor. Karen gabung ing Society for the Anthropology of North America (SANA)
