<doc id="146791" url="https://jv.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=146791" title="Stanley Diamond">
Stanley Diamond

Stanley Diamond ya iku ahli &lt;a href="antropologi"&gt;antropologi&lt;/a&gt; saka &lt;a href="New%20York"&gt;New York&lt;/a&gt; City, &lt;a href="Am%C3%A9rikah%20Sar%C3%A9kat"&gt;Amérikah Sarékat&lt;/a&gt;, kalairan 4 Januari 1922. Stanley olèh pandhidhikan saka New York University (BA) taun 1942. Sabanjuré ing Columbia University (Ph.D.) taun 1951. Dhèwèké naté nglakoni panlitian lapangan ana ing Dahomey (1951), &lt;a href="Israel"&gt;Israel&lt;/a&gt; (1951), &lt;a href="Nigeria"&gt;Nigeria&lt;/a&gt; (1963), Allegheny Seneca (1960), New York (1965), lan Biafra (1966). Stanley wis nulis werna-werna karya akademis kaya déné Primitive Views of the World: Essays from Culture in History (1964) minangka éditor, In Search of the Primitive: A Critique of Cvilization (1974), Totems (1982), lan Dahomy: Transition and Conflict in State Formation (1983). Kajiané Stanley ing bab tèori antropologi lan nerapké pandhangan meta-tèoritis ing sujarah antropologi, antropologi psikologi, antropologi pandhidhikan, antropologi bebrayan pra-nagara (pre-state societies), antropologi Utopia, ètnopoètik, lan Marxisme kulon (western Marxism).
