<doc id="147878" url="https://jv.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=147878" title="Edward Evan Evans-Pritchard">
Edward Evan Evans-Pritchard

Edward Evan Evans-Pritchard ya iku ahli &lt;a href="antropologi"&gt;antropologi&lt;/a&gt; saka Sussex, &lt;a href="Karajan%20Manunggal"&gt;Karajan Manunggal&lt;/a&gt;, kalairan taun 1902. Edward olèh pandhidhikan saka ing University of Oxford (MA) taun 1924 lan University of London, London School of Economics (Ph.D.) taun 1927. Dhéwéké nglakoni panlitian antropologis ing British-Mesir, &lt;a href="Sudan"&gt;Sudan&lt;/a&gt; (taun 1926), &lt;a href="Ethiopia"&gt;Ethiopia&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="Libya"&gt;Libya&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="Suriah"&gt;Suriah&lt;/a&gt;, lan wewengkon Wètan Tengah (1940 nganti 1944). Karya-karya akademis kang tinulis déning dhèwèké ya iku antarané Witchcraft, Oracles, and Magic among the Azande (1937), The Nuer: A Description of the Modes of Livelihood and Political Institutions of a Nilotic People (1940), The Sanusi of Cyrenaica (1949), lan Nuer Religion (1956). Edward iki misuwur amarga nggabungké kerangka téoritis Radcliffe-Brown lan &lt;a href="%C3%89mile%20Durkheim"&gt;Durkheim&lt;/a&gt; karo ètnografis empiris saka &lt;a href="Bronislaw%20Malinowski"&gt;Bronislaw Malinowski&lt;/a&gt;. Dhéwéké uga dadi salah siji antropolog kang ngedhasarké lan ngembangké antropologi sosial modèrn. Edward séda taun 1973 ana ing Oxford.
