<doc id="148002" url="https://jv.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=148002" title="Elizabeth Warnock Fernea">
Elizabeth Warnock Fernea

Elizabeth Warnock Fernea ya iku ahli &lt;a href="antropologi"&gt;antropologi&lt;/a&gt; wanita saka Milwaukee, Wisconsin, &lt;a href="Am%C3%A9rikah%20Sar%C3%A9kat"&gt;Amérikah Sarékat&lt;/a&gt;, kalairan tanggal 21 Oktober 1927. Pandhidhikan Elizabeth naté ing Reed College lan olih gelar BA taun 1949. Dhéwéké naté nglakoni panlitian lapangan antropologis ana ing &lt;a href="Irak"&gt;Irak&lt;/a&gt; (1956), &lt;a href="Mesir"&gt;Mesir&lt;/a&gt; (1962), &lt;a href="Maroko"&gt;Maroko&lt;/a&gt; (1971), &lt;a href="Yordania"&gt;Yordania&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="Libya"&gt;Libya&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="Lebanon"&gt;Lebanon&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="Yaman"&gt;Yaman&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="Israel"&gt;Israel&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="Palestina"&gt;Palestina&lt;/a&gt; (1983-1984 lan 1995-1996). Karya-karya akademis kang tinulis Elizabeth ya iku antarané Guests of the Sheik: An Ethnography of on Iraqi Village (1965), A Street in Marrakech (1975), Middle Eastern Muslim Women Speak (1977), lan The Arab World: Forty Years of Change (1997). Elizabeth iki nduwéni peranan penting nggawa bab Wetan Tengah marang kajian téori antropologi. Ing wewengkon wetan tengah, dhèwèké karenan ing bab wanita, kulawarga, lan bocah.
