<doc id="148003" url="https://jv.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=148003" title="Robert A. Fernea">
Robert A. Fernea

Robert Alan Fernea ya iku ahli &lt;a href="antropologi"&gt;antropologi&lt;/a&gt; saka Vancouver, Washington, &lt;a href="Am%C3%A9rikah%20Sar%C3%A9kat"&gt;Amérikah Sarékat&lt;/a&gt;, kalairan tanggal 25 Januari 1932. Pandhidhikané ing pawiyatan luhur naté ing Reed College (BA) taun 1954. Sabanjuré MA lan Ph.D. ing University of Chicacgo taun 1959. Robert nglakoni panlitian antropologis ana ing El Nahra, &lt;a href="Irak"&gt;Irak&lt;/a&gt; (1956), Nubia &lt;a href="Mesir"&gt;Mesir&lt;/a&gt; (1961), &lt;a href="Afghanistan"&gt;Afghanistan&lt;/a&gt; (1967), &lt;a href="Maroko"&gt;Maroko&lt;/a&gt; (1971), lan &lt;a href="Arab%20Saudi"&gt;Arab Saudi&lt;/a&gt; (1984). Karya-karya kang tinulis déning Robert ya iku antarané Shaykh and Effendi: Changing Patterns of Authority among the El-Shabana of Southern Iraq (1970), ‘Anthropology of the Middle East and North Africa: a critical assessment’ tinulis bareng James Malarkey, ana ing jurnal Annual Review of Anthropology (1975), lan The Arab World: Forty Years of Change (1997). Robert iki dadi ètnografer kang wis suwé nliti Wetan Tengah. Dhéwéké uga dadi guru lan komentator ing bab mau. Pisumbangan dhèwèké ya iku karya monograf bab Irak kidul lan Nubian Mesir. Robert iki bojo saka &lt;a href="Elizabeth%20Warnock%20Fernea"&gt;Elizabeth Warnock&lt;/a&gt;.
