<doc id="148216" url="https://jv.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=148216" title="P.H. Gulliver (Philip H.)">
P.H. Gulliver (Philip H.)

P.H. Gulliver (Philip H.) ya ik ahli &lt;a href="antropologi"&gt;antropologi&lt;/a&gt; saka Maldon, &lt;a href="Karajan%20Manunggal"&gt;Karajan Manunggal&lt;/a&gt;, kalairan ing tanggah 2 Sèptèmber 1921. Pandhidhikan ing pawiyatan luhur naté ana ing &lt;a href="University%20of%20London"&gt;University of London&lt;/a&gt; (B.Sc.) ing taun 1947. Sabanjuré ing &lt;a href="London%20School%20of%20Economics"&gt;London School of Economics&lt;/a&gt; (Ph.D.) ing taun 1952. Panlitian lapangan antropologis sing linakoni déning dhèwèké ya iku ana ing &lt;a href="Kenya"&gt;Kenya&lt;/a&gt; (taun 1948), &lt;a href="Uganda"&gt;Uganda&lt;/a&gt; (taun 1950-1951), &lt;a href="Tanzania"&gt;Tanzania&lt;/a&gt; (taun 1952 ganti 1954), Arusha (1956), lan Shona, Rhodesia (taun 1961). Karya-karya akademis sing sinerat déning Philip Gulliver ya iku The Family Herds: A Study of Two Pastoral Tribes in East Africa (taun 1955), Neighbours and Networks: The Idiom of Kinship among the Ndendeuli (taun 1971), Disputes and Negotiations: A Cross-Cultural Perspective (taun 1979), lan Merchants and Shopkeepers: A Historical Anthropology of an Irish Market Town, sinerat bareng karo Marilyn Silverman (taun 1995). Philip iki duwé pisumbangané ing pangembangan téoritis lan métodhologi ètnografi.
